1
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:34,300
These categories or themes need not be of the same type.

2
00:03:34,740 --> 00:03:42,660
They can be about objects, processes, differences, similarities, emotions or basically anything.

3
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:49,240
Your work process now, compared to previous steps, is more general and abstract.

4
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:58,060
The categories you create, which also become the main result of the study, must be of general interest to your future readers.

5
00:03:58,260 --> 00:04:04,680
Step 4. Name your categories, determined which are most relevant and how they belong together.

6
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:10,100
Name the categories.
In my example, I have three categories or themes.

7
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:18,260
I call the first constant adaptation, the second information search and the third problem solving.

8
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:24,500
In my case there were three categories, but it could just as well have been two or four.

9
00:04:26,040 --> 00:04:31,060
You should also describe how the categories and their content are interconnected.
